name: Timeline Entry
description: >
  Immutable entry in an append-only Timeline. The Timeline Provider assigns a
  timestamp that is unique and strictly increasing within the timeline, links
  the entry to its predecessor, and authenticates actor and available source
  attribution. A feeder validates, orders, and filters entries before passing
  eligible events to a processor.

timeline:
  type: Coordination/Timeline
  schema:
    required: true
  description: Timeline containing this entry.

prevEntry:
  type: Coordination/Timeline Entry
  description: >
    Previous entry in the same timeline, normally represented as a pure
    reference. The first entry may omit this field.

timestamp:
  type: Integer
  schema:
    required: true
  description: >
    Microsecond timestamp assigned by the Timeline Provider. It is unique and
    strictly increasing within this timeline and is the authoritative
    intra-timeline ordering value. It also supports cross-timeline ordering and
    completeness windows under the provider profile.

actor:
  type: Coordination/Actor
  schema:
    required: true
  description: Actor attributed as the writer or submitter of this entry.

source:
  type: Coordination/Source
  description: >
    Optional provider-authenticated attribution of how the entry was submitted,
    such as through a browser session, API call, or document request. Source
    complements actor attribution and does not grant authority by itself. A
    policy that requires or excludes a source category must treat an absent
    source as not satisfying that source constraint.

onBehalfOf:
  type: Coordination/Authority
  description: >
    Optional authority under which actor claims to act for another actor. A
    feeder validates the concrete authority before delivery when the requested
    action is not directly eligible through a source channel. Mandate-backed
    authority uses Mandate/Mandate Authority.

message:
  schema:
    required: true
  description: Message or event recorded by the entry.
